# Answer key for B8 t1_breadth.sql - procedural PL/pgSQL, breadth.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: all earlier decisions, the Oracle procedural conventions (OBJECTIVES.md
# rules 1-9), plus D-39..D-42 (decided 2026-10-04, not implemented). Variables are
# `var:<name>`. Bands per edge (rule 5). Origin unit = the routine.
# NOT EXPRESSIBLE IN A KEY, CHECKED IN THE REPORT: every CREATE FUNCTION / PROCEDURE /
# TRIGGER, S2 and S4 and S21 (calls), and the R11 definition give no edge of their own and
# are not refused for being procedural; a routine the analyser cannot read is refused or
# declared, never partially analysed.

@ 22 S1 a function body's static INSERT
origin mart.fn_load_channel 0
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.channel identity
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.channel_mix.revenue aggregated
influence staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.revenue
filter staging.orders.status -> mart.channel_mix

@ 41 S3 a parameter in WHERE
origin mart.pr_region 0
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue aggregated
influence core.dim_store.region -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue
filter core.dim_store.region -> mart.kpi_rollup
origin mart.pr_region 1
filter var:mart.pr_region.p_region -> mart.kpi_rollup
note A parameter on the path is band 1 (Oracle: stress_merge_upsert's P_REGION).

@ 62 S5 SELECT ... INTO a variable
origin mart.fn_pay_total 1
value staging.payments.amount -> var:mart.fn_pay_total.v_total aggregated
filter staging.payments.status -> staging.payments
note The statement writes a variable, so its filter targets the relation read (rule 2).

@ 66 S6 an assignment
origin mart.fn_pay_total 1
value var:mart.fn_pay_total.v_total -> var:mart.fn_pay_total.v_rate derived

@ 68 S7 the variables as values
origin mart.fn_pay_total 1
value var:mart.fn_pay_total.v_rate -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue identity
value var:mart.fn_pay_total.v_total -> mart.kpi_rollup.orders identity

@ 85 S8 the loop body: the record is transparent
origin mart.fn_loop_cust 1
value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.customer_summary.full_name identity
filter staging.customers.status -> mart.customer_summary
filter staging.customers.id -> mart.customer_summary
filter mart.customer_summary.customer_id -> mart.customer_summary
note The loop query's WHERE decides which rows the body ever sees (rule 4); r.id is c.id.

@ 103 S9 FETCH into variables
origin mart.fn_cursor_store 1
value core.dim_store.id -> var:mart.fn_cursor_store.v_store_id identity
value core.dim_store.name -> var:mart.fn_cursor_store.v_store_name identity
filter core.dim_store.status -> core.dim_store

@ 105 S10 the fetched variables as values
origin mart.fn_cursor_store 1
value var:mart.fn_cursor_store.v_store_id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id identity
value var:mart.fn_cursor_store.v_store_name -> mart.sales_daily.region identity

@ 127 S11 reading a RETURN QUERY function: inlined (D-40)
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.top_customers.revenue identity
filter staging.orders.status, staging.orders.channel -> mart.top_customers
note p_ch takes the literal 'web': no edge. o.channel = p_ch still filters.

@ 139 S12 SELECT INTO inside a scalar function
origin mart.fn_cust_value 1
value staging.orders.amount -> var:mart.fn_cust_value.v_value aggregated
filter staging.orders.customer_id -> staging.orders
filter var:mart.fn_cust_value.p_cust -> staging.orders

@ 147 S13 a scalar function in a query
value staging.customers.id -> mart.customer_summary.customer_id identity
origin <script> 1
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.customer_summary.lifetime_value aggregated
note Rule 6: the columns the return value depends on, band 1.
forbid value staging.customers.id -> mart.customer_summary.lifetime_value | c.id is only the function's argument (Oracle: fn_stress_net)

@ 158 S14 a DO block
origin <do> 0
value staging.events_log.id -> mart.events_log.id identity
value staging.events_log.kind -> mart.events_log.kind identity
filter staging.events_log.payload_size -> mart.events_log

@ 172 S15 constant dynamic SQL
origin <do> 2
value staging.customers.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
filter staging.customers.country_code -> mart.kpi_rollup

@ 183 S16 format() of constants
origin <do> 2
value staging.customers.country_code -> mart.kpi_rollup.country_code identity

@ 195 S17 EXECUTE of a parameter
expect dynamic_sql EXECUTE:195 | the table name is p_table, a parameter: undecidable (D-42)

@ 207 S18 a trigger on INSERT: NEW
origin mart.trg_order_audit 2
value staging.orders.id -> mart.events_log.id identity
value staging.orders.status -> mart.events_log.kind identity

@ 225 S19 a trigger on UPDATE: OLD
origin mart.trg_pay_history 2
value staging.payments.order_id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value staging.payments.amount -> mart.top_customers.revenue identity

@ 243 S20 an UPDATE then COMMIT in a procedure
origin mart.pr_close_stores 0
filter core.dim_store.opened_on -> core.dim_store

@ 262 S22a RETURN NEXT of a SETOF text routine
origin mart.fn_gen_regions 1
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.fn_gen_regions.fn_gen_regions identity
note semantic-ir T3/T10 (2026-10-18): rows built by RETURN NEXT go into the routine's output relation, one column named after the function (PostgreSQL's own name for SETOF a base type). Until then declared source_unavailable (D-40).

@ 268 S22 reading a RETURN NEXT function
value mart.fn_gen_regions.fn_gen_regions -> mart.channel_mix.region identity

@ 280 S23 the protected statement
origin mart.fn_upsert_ledger 0
value staging.ledger.id -> core.ledger.id identity
value staging.ledger.account -> core.ledger.account identity

@ 284 S24 the handler's statement
origin mart.fn_upsert_ledger 0
value core.ledger.balance -> core.ledger.balance derived
filter core.ledger.status -> core.ledger

@ 298 S25 a write, then GET DIAGNOSTICS
origin mart.fn_count_rows 0
filter staging.events_log.kind -> mart.events_log

@ 302 S26 the count as a value
origin mart.fn_count_rows 1
value var:mart.fn_count_rows.v_rows -> mart.kpi_rollup.customers identity
note GET DIAGNOSTICS gives v_rows no column source; the variable still reaches the column (rule 3).
